{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_018Q6YLNfCUsVxVG1Unv1tta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **`answers/04-006-design-a-model-for-math-problems-data-sft-post-training-eval.md`** — the answer for Q6: *Design a model for math problems — data, SFT, post-training, eval.*\n\nThe note covers:\n\n- **Data phase** — GSM8K + MATH public datasets + synthetic CoT via GPT-4o with rejection sampling (how DeepSeek-Math/Qwen-Math scale cheaply); every example is a `(problem, scratchpad, \\boxed{answer})` triple\n- **SFT phase** — LoRA rank 32–64 on Llama 3 8B / Qwen2.5-Math-7B, cross-entropy over the *full* response (scratchpad + answer) to teach reasoning format; ~75–80% GSM8K pass@1\n- **Post-training** — DPO (offline, simple, correct/incorrect pairs) vs PRM + GRPO (step-level process reward, used in o1 / DeepSeek-R1, more robust for competition bar)\n- **Eval** — pass@1, maj@8, MATH Level 3–5, held-out domain set; sub-domain breakdown to catch algebraic vs combinatorics collapse\n- **Concrete example** — Qwen2.5-Math-7B-Instruct achieving 95.2% GSM8K / 83.6% MATH via synthetic CoT + ORM-guided MCTS + DPO\n\nNext up: **Q7 — Scalable efficient LLM training system — compute and data constraints.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":65338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":393,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40646904-0a51-45b3-a326-56666fea64f2","uuid":"4a6682c4-1798-4307-8854-4bb7a321f140"}
